          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of algebra modality is used to define
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+categories"} codifferential categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrines"} categorical doctrines
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+modality"} algebra modality
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, I)
              is given by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,m,u)
              and two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta:I \rightarrow S(A)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
